The two runs that sent a request printed the "Checking the API: sending one minimal request to <host>..." line first.

Real-host risk: the integration tests that run yoyo doctor go through yoyo_cmd, which removes every *_API_KEY variable. So they get the no-key result and never contact a real vendor. The ollama test only touches localhost.

Tests: all against a stub on 127.0.0.1. They cover 200, 401, 403, 404, 500, a closed port, a server that never answers, and a check that the key goes only in its header and only to the stub's host. Each asserts the full message text.

